title: A top-down adventure
intro: A dark dungeon lit by your lantern, a key, a locked door and a treasure behind it, all built from the Entity menu and the Inspector.
summary: Build a small top-down dungeon from an empty project: a hero with a lantern, walls that cast shadows, a key and a locked door, a treasure and a bat.
project: Empty | Dungeon

chapter: A hero with a lantern | Entity > Characters > Top-down Player
say: A top-down game looks down on the world, so there is no gravity and the hero moves in eight directions. Start from the Empty template and make the hero.
deselect
create: Top-down Player
expectcomponents: Player = Transform, Sprite, BoxCollider, Body, TopDownMovement
say: The Body has Gravity Scale 0, and Top Down Movement reads the arrow keys, WASD or the stick. Now make the room dark and give the hero a light to see by.
add: Light
set: Light.Radius = 5
set: Light.Shadows = true
select: Main Camera
set: Camera.Size = 6
set: Camera.Ambient = #4A5270
say: A camera's Ambient color is the light a scene has everywhere. A dark blue one makes the room dim, and any Light brightens the part it reaches. With Shadows on, walls block it.
shot: lantern

chapter: Walls | Sprites with colliders
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Wall
set: Transform.Position = 0, 5, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 20, 1
set: Sprite.Tint = #484B55
add: BoxCollider
set: BoxCollider.Size = 20, 1
say: A wall is a sprite with a box collider. Make one, then copy it with Ctrl+D and move and resize each copy.
key: Ctrl+D
set: Transform.Position = 0, -5, 0
key: Ctrl+D
set: Transform.Position = -10, 0, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 1, 10
set: BoxCollider.Size = 1, 10
key: Ctrl+D
set: Transform.Position = 10, 0, 0
expectcount: Wall = 4
say: Four walls make a room. Press F5 and walk into them: the hero stops, and the lantern's light stops at the walls too.
shot: walls

chapter: A locked door | A Switch that wants a key
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Divider Top
set: Transform.Position = 3, 3.25, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 0.5, 2.5
set: Sprite.Tint = #484B55
add: BoxCollider
set: BoxCollider.Size = 0.5, 2.5
key: Ctrl+D
rename: Divider Bottom
set: Transform.Position = 3, -3.25, 0
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Door
set: Transform.Position = 3, 0, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 0.5, 4
set: Sprite.Tint = #E3B341
add: BoxCollider
set: BoxCollider.Size = 0.5, 4
add: Switch
set: Switch.Mode = Button
set: Switch.Key = Key
set: Switch.Hides = Door
expectcomponents: Door = Transform, Sprite, BoxCollider, Switch
say: A wall with a gap in it, closed by a door. A Switch in Button mode turns on when something touches it, and one that has a Key only turns on for someone carrying that item. While it is on, it hides everything it names in Hides, and here that is the door itself.
shot: door

chapter: The key and the treasure | Pickup with an Item
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Key
set: Transform.Position = -3, 0, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 0.35, 0.6
set: Sprite.Tint = #E3B341
add: CircleCollider
set: CircleCollider.Is Trigger = true
add: Pickup
set: Pickup.Layers = Player
set: Pickup.Item = Key
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Treasure
set: Transform.Position = 5.5, 0, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 0.5, 0.5
set: Sprite.Tint = #57AB5A
add: CircleCollider
set: CircleCollider.Is Trigger = true
add: Pickup
set: Pickup.Layers = Player
set: Pickup.Amount = 5
say: A Pickup with an Item puts it in the hero's pockets when they touch it. The key is that item, so the door will open for whoever picked it up. The treasure is worth five points.
deselect
create: Text
rename: Score
set: Transform.Position = -8, 4, 0
set: Text.Value = Score: 0
add: Counter
shot: pickups

chapter: A bat | Chase
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Bat
set: Transform.Position = 8, 3.5, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 0.7, 0.5
set: Sprite.Tint = #9B6BD6
add: Chase
set: Chase.Range = 3
set: Chase.Needs Sight = true
add: DamageOnTouch
set: DamageOnTouch.Layers = Player
select: Player
add: Health
say: A Chase follows the hero once it is near and can see them, and gives up when they get away. Needs Sight makes the walls hide the hero from it. The hero needs Health to be hurt, three hits by default.
expectcomponents: Bat = Transform, Sprite, BoxCollider, Body, Chase, DamageOnTouch
shot: bat

chapter: Play it | Key, door, treasure
play
wait: 0.8
wait: 1
hold: Right 3
expectat: Player = 2.35, 0
say: Run for the door first and it stays shut: the hero has no key yet.
hold: Left 6
wait: 0.3
say: Fetch the key from the left of the room.
hold: Right 10
wait: 1
expectvalue: Score.Text.Value = Score: 6
say: With the key the door opens as the hero touches it, and the treasure is theirs: one point for the key, which scores like any pickup, and five for the treasure.
shot: playing | game | 960
stop
say: That is a small adventure. Add Dialogue Boxes for talking, portals between rooms, and more rooms of your own, each a scene.
